From 6e127609275b4e3f2dac364c89b4e3654c7065a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Hutsaliuk <artemgutsaliukv@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 02:51:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 158/194] pinctrl: qcom: sm7150-lpass-lpi: fix swr_rx_data mux
 value on GPIO5

The second SoundWire RX data line has the same off-by-one slot as GPIO1
had for TX: the vendor device tree programs func2 for gpio23, while
listing swr_rx_data third in LPI_PINGROUP() makes the driver select 3.

This one hides better than the TX case. The RX bus enumerates either way
and the codec attaches, so everything looks healthy until playback data
actually flows - the controller then raises MASTER_CLASH_DET and the
stream dies after a fraction of a second. On a device whose loudspeaker
hangs off an external amplifier and not off the codec, that can go
unnoticed for a long time: the earpiece is the only thing behind the RX
bus.

Tested on a Xiaomi Mi 9T (SM7150-AA, WCD9375): before, playback to the
earpiece produced a short burst and silence, with bit 3 set in the
controller's interrupt status; after, the clash is gone and the earpiece
plays cleanly.

Signed-off-by: Artem Hutsaliuk <artemgutsaliukv@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
index 0b268ac08..c3cb508e6 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -92,6 +92,14 @@ static const struct lpi_pingroup sm7150_groups[] = {
 	LPI_PINGROUP(2, 4, slimbus_data, swr_tx_data, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(3, 8, slimbus_data, swr_rx_clk, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(4, 10, slimbus_data, swr_rx_data, prim_mclk_a, _),
+	/*
+	 * Same off-by-one slot as GPIO1 above, on the second SoundWire RX data
+	 * line: the vendor tree programs func2 for gpio23, while listing
+	 * swr_rx_data third here makes the driver select 3. The bus enumerates
+	 * either way, so this only shows up once playback data actually flows -
+	 * the controller then reports MASTER_CLASH_DET and the stream dies
+	 * after a fraction of a second.
+	 */
 	LPI_PINGROUP(5, 6, qua_mi2s_sclk, swr_rx_data, _, swr_tx_data),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(6, LPI_NO_SLEW, qua_mi2s_ws, cdc_pdm_rx, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(7, LPI_NO_SLEW, qua_mi2s_data, _, _, _),
